  "title": "CHAPTER 6: CONTROL & COORDINATION",
  "order": 6,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "vbl8n8x",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Introduction"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The nervous system and endocrine system jointly coordinate body functions in animals.",
        "Neurons transmit electrical signals from dendrites through the axon to synapses.",
        "The brain and spinal cord constitute the Central Nervous System (CNS).",
        "Plant growth and directional movements are regulated by phytohormones like Auxin, Gibberellin, Cytokinin, ABA, and Ethylene."
      ],
      "id": "9kmqljk"
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
        {
          "label": "Functional Unit",
          "value": "Neuron",
